1. Install a python version that works with pygame, use python versions below 3.14
2. Install .venv with requirements.txt, In vs studio its 'Ctrl Shift P' then python > create environment
3. Run in terminal 'python -m game.main' from the root folder

This got a bit more structure but still alpha version, v0.0.1 or something

I've put some comments but its currently working so that you can setup any environment you want to work I believe
To make 'new levels' go to environments/base.py and use the base class, the setup and loop in there are called in window/display.py
To make add elements to the screen you have to draw them to the screen, in elements/sprite.py there are functions for updating (for example position) or drawing (like a triangle) for each sprite, then in the environment level you call for them to be updated or whatever you want to do to them

Obviously if you don't like some things feel free to change it cause this is just my way of thinking how to implement our game